; `word-wide` WITHOUT A RENDERER: the cube returned as the target's own integer.
;
; On Go, the JVM and windows the result range [0, 2^63−1] is the word, so the
; value is a machine integer and each host prints it natively — this is the case
; that covers windows, where `word-wide` cannot render. JavaScript is skipped
; for a reason that is about printing and not about the integer: there the value
; is a BigInt, and `console.log` presents one as `343n` (targets/js/bigint.oro).
; `word-wide` checks the same integers on JavaScript through `big-str`.
; skip: js
;
; inputs: 0 1 7 1000000 999999 2097151
; expect: 0 1 343 1000000000000000000 999997000002999999 9223358842721533951

(sig cube ((n (int 0 2097151))) (int 0 9223372036854775807))

(def cube (n) (* (* n n) n))

(def run (n) (cube n))
